 * The first revision re-threw every non-1 exit status. In CI that crashed the
 * daily sweep instead of reporting a finding: #2273's merge commit exists only
 * on a deleted branch, so a fresh clone has no such object and `git merge-base
 * --is-ancestor` exits 128, not 1. It passed locally only because the
 * investigating clone had already fetched that object by hand.
